<div class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>About PornProxy</h1><p>An honest tool for an annoying problem.</p></div></div>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
<p>PornProxy started with a simple frustration: adult sites get blocked all the time - by internet providers, by countries, by school and office networks - and the "solutions" are usually a VPN subscription or sketchy free proxy covered in pop-ups.</p>
<p>We thought there should be a middle option: a clean, free web proxy that just works. Paste a URL, get the page. No account, no install, no upsell maze. So we built one.</p>
<h2>What we believe</h2>
<p><strong>Adults should be able to reach legal content.</strong> Whatever you think of porn, blocking it at the network level is a blunt instrument - and adults find workarounds anyway. We'd rather the workaround be safe and straightforward than shady.</p>
<p><strong>Tools should be honest about their limits.</strong> A web proxy hides your IP from the site you visit, but it doesn't hide your traffic from your internet provider, and it can't move its own server to another country. We say that plainly on every page, because a tool you misunderstand is a tool that can burn you.</p>
<p><strong>Free shouldn't mean hostile.</strong> No fake download buttons, no "your Flash player is outdated" traps, no selling your data. The site is supported simply - and if it ever isn't, we'd rather shut a feature down than turn hostile.</p>
<h2>How the site is run</h2>
<p>PornProxy is a small independent project. The proxy engine is our own code (PHP, no third-party proxy services in the loop), the guides on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a> are written by us, and the <a href="/privacy-policy.php">privacy policy</a> is short enough to actually read.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
